[COMMENTS]
STATION,Station built to improve flood warning in the Clyde catchment. GENERAL: Velocity area station, the most upstream on the Clyde. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10). STATION HYDROMETRY: Station spills into right floodplain after around 2m and then into left floodplain after around 2.8m. Rating based on gaugings up to ~1.6m and thereafter higher flow estimates are informed by velocity indexing from a fixed ADCP and floodplain modelling. FLOW REGIME: Two major reservoirs in the catchment.
CATCHMENT,Heavily grazed uplands and heather moor. Large wind farms have been installed in the catchment since the station was built.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Although there are few gaugings above QMED, ratings takes into account out of bank flow.
[END]
